DTEND:20260725T180000Z
SUMMARY:Mirror Or Window
DESCRIPTION:Some images reflect what we already know\, others reveal something new. In this interactive experience\, artworks are explored as shifting viewpoints. Certain scenes echo familiar memories\, while others introduce different ways of living and seeing the world. Through guided observation and creative response\, children interpret what they see and translate it into visual expression. The experience results in personal interpretations shaped by both recognition and discovery.
LOCATION:Ithra - Museum - Gallery 3
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-mirror-or-window.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-our-place-on-earth@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260710T130000Z
DTEND:20260725T180000Z
SUMMARY:Our Place on Earth
DESCRIPTION:A house in the desert is not built like one by the sea\, and for good reason. In this experience\, children explore how homes respond to their environments\, from heat to movement to moisture. This leads into building and testing simple structures\, adjusting them to stand against different conditions.
LOCATION:Ithra - Energy Exhibit
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-our-place-on-earth.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-painted-faces@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260710T130000Z
DTEND:20260725T180000Z
SUMMARY:Painted Faces
DESCRIPTION:What's a festival without facepainting? Children choose from a variety of designs and have them painted using safe\, child-friendly colors.
LOCATION:Ithra - Children's Museum
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-painted-faces.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-where-we-belong@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260710T130000Z
DTEND:20260725T180000Z
SUMMARY:Where We Belong
DESCRIPTION:Look closely at Earth\, and it begins to feel like a system that never stops working\; air moving\, water cycling\, living things adapting. In this program\, children explore how life continues and changes across different environments\, and how organisms adjust to survive over time. The journey then stretches further\, looking at how science studies these systems and reimagines them beyond Earth. The experience connects life\, environment\, and possibility in one continuous story.
LOCATION:Ithra - Energy Exhibit
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-where-we-belong.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-zoom-in@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260710T130000Z
DTEND:20260725T180000Z
SUMMARY:Zoom In
DESCRIPTION:A tiny fragment holds the clue. In this Praise of the Artisan treasure hunt\, children begin with a zoomed-in detail taken from a larger artwork\, a pattern\, texture\, or small visual hint. Moving through the space\, they search for the full piece\, matching what they see up close with what appears on the walls. As the search unfolds\, attention shifts to details that are often overlooked\, building observation skills through careful looking. Each match reveals the complete artwork behind the fragment.
LOCATION:Ithra - Museum - Gallery 3
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-zoom-in.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-in-the-home-of@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260710T133000Z
DTEND:20260725T180000Z
SUMMARY:In the Home of…
DESCRIPTION:Some homes are easy to recognize. Others leave clues behind. In this interactive library experience\, children move through a series of spaces\, each one arranged as a &ldquo\;home&rdquo\; shaped by a well-known literary character. Objects\, layouts\, and small details hint at who might live there. As they explore each corner\, children follow prompts and challenges that guide them to observe\, connect\, and identify the character behind each space. The experience unfolds step by step\, turning the library into a trail of clues where stories are discovered through place\, detail\, and interaction.
LOCATION:Ithra - Library - Level 2
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-in-the-home-of.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:event-my-little-fort@eventme.live
DTSTAMP:20260710T131814Z
DTSTART:20260710T140000Z
DTEND:20260725T183000Z
SUMMARY:My Little Fort
DESCRIPTION:Many children create small spaces of their own at home&mdash\;under a table\, behind cushions\, or inside a blanket fort. In this hands-on activity\, children build their own small &ldquo\;fort&rdquo\; using soft materials\, shaping a space they can define and arrange. The session ends with a short story connected to the idea of shared spaces and home.
LOCATION:Ithra - Children's Museum
URL:https://eventme.live/events/event-my-little-fort.html
END:VEVENT
